      "message": "Thanks for the great analysis and I like where this implementation is going. But I think sharing global cache wouldn\u0027t go well if you are working on multiple repos at the same time because running `git cl presubmit` will invalidate the cache all the other repos.\n\nI like the idea of a separate file for caching but I also think it\u0027s better to have a per-repo cache. How about using a temp file as cache and store that path in git config (e.g. depot_tools.gerrit_cache.path\u003d/path/to/temp). For non-git environment, we could teach it to read the path from some env var(our start-up script in Cog could be responsible for setting the path).\n\nAlso, can we move the implementation to [here](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/tools/depot_tools/+/main:presubmit_support.py;l\u003d598-602;drc\u003d2e88a3f08bd8c4a0014eae82729beca935f7f188) because we can now retire the in-process cache and I think it might be useful to leave gerrit_util module just purely talk to Gerrit",
